result: 'Made send-after-close observable. jinn_chan_send now returns int (1=delivered,
  0=closed/dropped); codegen exposes it as a bool. `send ch, v` / `ch.send(v)` now
  type as bool: bind it (`ok is send ch, v`) to observe delivery, ignore it for fire-and-forget
  (actor async-sends unchanged). Docs (concurrency.md) updated: ops table, closed-channel
  semantics, sharp-edge #4, testing table. Added conformance tests send_after_close_is_observable
  + bare_send_ignores_result. Full suite green, zero warnings.'
description: Make sends after channel close produce a defined, observable error/result
  rather than silent loss or panic. Depends on concurrency model. Done when behavior
  is documented and tested.
